[z0w3116@venus.tamu.edu (WU, ZUOGUO) writes:]
[] What exactly does ring of warning do? I noticed that when it glows some
[] colors, usually there is a monster nearby. Do the different colors have
[] some meaning?

[brajesh@en.ecn.purdue.edu (Brajesh K Singh) writes:]
[] It glows whem there is a powerful monster arround.
[] The colors go from light to dark. Depending upon the power of the monster.

no, wait ... there's more ...

as you say, the colors are coded from light (white) to dark (black)
and indicate the _relative_ threat of the monster to you.  the system
is non-intuitive and, simply put, needs to be scrapped in favor of
something that makes sense!  it would be nice if the warning colors
somehow directly corresponded to certain monsters ...

[zuoguo:]
[] I once gave a lot of money (4800) to the temple priest. The priest said
[] that I had been rewarded. I noticed that my AC went down by two. Is that
[] permanent? If so, can you do it twice?

[brajesh:]
[] Yes it is quite permanent, and yes you can do it twice but the chances are
[] slim. 

well no, ... the AC benefit that you got will not go away unless you cause
it to go away (which can happen).  you can easily get this effect again
and again but the math involved may be hard to figure out.  personally
i don't think any normal person can figure it out without spoilers ...

[zuoguo:]
[] Is there any way to kill a dragon without resistance? My last character
[] killed gray dragon, white dragon, but was killed by a red dragon.

[brajesh:]
[] You don't need resistance to fight them, but it would be helpful to have
[] it just incase you got blasted by one.

dragons will not use their breath attacks if they are directly
adjacent to you and can simply pound on you.  you can use this to
your advantage ...

[zuoguo:]
